        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(auto-reply): support custom silent tokens with digits and punctuation in prefix matcher",
        "body": "Fixes #99982\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`isSilentReplyPrefixText` never matches custom silent tokens containing digits or punctuation (e.g., `NOREPLY2`, `NO-ANSWER`). The character guard `/[^A-Z_]/.test(normalized)` at L304 of `src/auto-reply/tokens.ts` rejects any input containing non-letter characters, causing streamed prefix detection to fail for custom tokens with digits/hyphens.\n\nThis means the streaming suppression path effectively ignores custom silent tokens that include numbers or special characters.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe character guard was too broad — it checked the **input fragment** (the streamed prefix) instead of the **token definition**. An input fragment is inherently transient and partial; the only meaningful question is whether the token itself is safe for prefix matching.\n\n- Custom tokens containing non-letter characters (digits, hyphens) cannot be mistaken for natural language words, so their partial prefixes are safe.\n- The underscore guard (`normalized.includes(\"_\")`) is preserved for standard `A-Z_` tokens like `HEARTBEAT_OK`.\n- The `/[^A-Z_]/.test(tokenUpper)` check now tests the **token**, not the fragment.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBefore: custom silent tokens like `\"NOREPLY2\"` or `\"NO-ANSWER\"` never match in the streaming prefix matcher, delaying silent-reply classification until the full token is received.\n\nAfter: prefix fragments of custom tokens (e.g., `\"NORE\"` for `\"NOREPLY2\"`, `\"NO-AN\"` for `\"NO-ANSWER\"`) are correctly recognized during streaming.\n\nAll 42 tests pass (original 39 + 3 new).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Implementation: `src/auto-reply/tokens.ts`\n- Tests: `src/auto-reply/tokens.test.ts`\n- Test suite: `pnpm test src/auto-reply/tokens.test.ts` — 42 passed\n- `git diff --numstat`: 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n\n## AI Assistance\n\nThis commit was co-authored with AI. The AI implemented the fix, tests, and PR description under human supervision. See `https://docs.openclaw.ai/contributing/ai` for AI contribution policy.",
